test_changes:
No existing test or assertion was removed or weakened, and dsa/bench/tree.bench.ts is unchanged. Additions only:
1. dsa/tests/tree.test.ts: 7 new unit tests appended after the original 20:
   - detaching a non-empty directory with a hard link out of it drops its subtree from size, and the subtree can be grafted back;
   - attach refuses the root, an ancestor, itself, a second link to a directory, and invalid names (including the 255/256-byte astral boundary), with NOT_LOADED on an unloaded target;
   - a graft containing a cycle or a live directory is refused and changes nothing;
   - move reports NOT_FOUND, NOT_LOADED and INVALID for a bad name, and a file move keeps size;
   - unload updates size, keeps files hard-linked elsewhere, handles an unloaded walk start and unloading the root;
   - setLoaded checks every entry before installing any and grafts a preloaded subdirectory;
   - checkInvariants names T1, T3, T5 and T6.
2. dsa/tests/tree.prop.test.ts:
   - one new property checking name validation against TextEncoder over arbitrary strings, including surrogate pairs and lone surrogates;
   - a per-test timeout of max(5 s, 20 ms x PROP.numRuns) on the file's three property tests. Vitest's default 5 s cannot hold the nightly 10,000 runs of spec §8 (about 17-20 s here) and was exceeded at 1,000 runs under parallel load (8 s observed). The assertions are unchanged.
